description: Docs stay declarative. Infrastructure is a diagram, not an essay.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Docs

- A document states a fact. It does not narrate how the fact was chosen.
- One heading, then the statement. No multi-paragraph lead-in.
- Infrastructure is a diagram. Text under it names a box or a rule.
- A document longer than two screens is split or cut.
- A mandatory requirement is not written up as an omission.
- Follow docs/conventions.md.
